      ['How many chromosomes does an ordinary human cell contain?', '46 (23 pairs)', [['23', 'That is the number in sex cells. 🥚'], ['2', 'Far more. 🔢'], ['100', 'Too many. 🔢']], 'Chromosomes, in the nucleus, carry the genetic information.'],
      ['How does a vaccine work?', 'it prepares the immune system to recognise a microbe', [['it kills every microbe in the body', 'That is not its role. 🦠'], ['it replaces the immune system', 'It trains it. 💪'], ['it cures a disease you already have', 'It prevents rather than cures. 🛡️']], 'A vaccine creates immune memory: if the microbe turns up, the response is fast and effective.']
